I've left out the enrichment fetch. The node's grant here is only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so the world imports nothing else. The node drops every item whose `id` is already present in the `seen` store and returns the rest in their original order.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

